<title>USA: Donnelley sees 1996 oper EPS $1.45-$1.55.</title>
<headline>Donnelley sees 1996 oper EPS $1.45-$1.55.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>R.R. Donnelley &amp; Sons Co said on Thursday it expects to report earnings of $1.45 to $1.55 per share, excluding certain extraordinary items, for the full year 1996.  </p>
<p>The items excluded are a gain of $44 million pre-tax, or $26 million after-tax, on the initial public offering of Metromail Corp in the second quarter, and a pre-tax restructuring charge of $560 million, or $435 million after-taxes and minority interest benefit, in the first half.</p>
<p>&quot;Excluding the restructuring charges and the Metromail gain, the company expects to earn between $1.45 and $1.55 per share for the year,&quot; said the publishing giant.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
